Let heights be a list of 2, 1, 5, 6, 2, and 3.
Let last be the last position of heights.
Let best be 0.
For every left from 0 to last.
Let minimum be item left of heights.
For every right from left to last.
If item right of heights is less than minimum, set minimum to item right of heights.
Let area be minimum times (right minus left plus 1).
If area is more than best, set best to area.

Print best.
